Similarly, within the `else if` block, TypeScript knows that `value` is definitely a `number`, and so it infers the type of `numValue` as `number`.

By using type narrowing techniques like these, you can provide more specific type information to TypeScript, even when working with values that may have multiple types. This helps to improve code quality and prevent runtime errors.

